Negative control for the one-writer mitigation at a scope call site (T2.2,
design §7.3, `AC9.1`).

Pushes the bare `buildScopePath` result, the shape every scope selector in this
tree carried before `usePlaygroundUrlState` existed (`useScopeNavigation`'s own
`router.push(path)`). Scope is the router's and surface state is history's, so
a router push rebuilds the query from the location it is handed: `view`,
`track`, `scene`, `sheet`, `tab` and `force` are silently dropped by a brand
switch. Nothing throws, the navigation lands, the brand changes — the link a
colleague was sent simply stops reproducing the surface.

The mutant removes the writer's import and binding too, so the patched tree
still lints: the defect must be the dropped query, not an unused symbol.

